WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.800
Take a look around the solar system.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.240
Eight planets orbiting a central star.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.820
The Sun. Among them is Earth.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.670
And its neighbor, Venus.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.510
Earth. Our home is an oasis for life.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:23.560
And Venus.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.900
That's the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.460
Venus and Earth couldn't be more different.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.920
The earth is this beautiful planet and
there's water everywhere.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.060
It's ice at the poles.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.260
It's water in the ocean.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.630
It's in the atmosphere as water vapor.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.410
But then you look at Venus.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.020
It is the worst place imaginable.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.740
It is so hot on the surface.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.960
Crushing pressures.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.560
It couldn't be any less supportive of life.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.710
To me, the planet Venus is sort of a classic
definition of the word hell.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:06.280
If you were to transport to Venus and
experience the environment there, you'd

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.290
quickly want to return back to Earth.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:14.560
The conditions on Venus are among the most
inhospitable in the solar system.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.810
It's just a horrible place.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.520
It's so hot and there's no water in the
atmosphere is so thick and it rains sulfuric

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.120
acid.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.770
It's going to be a competition between
whether or not you're going to be cooked to

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.210
death or crushed to death.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.640
Earth. And Venus may seem like very different
worlds.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.330
But they shouldn't.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:51.310
They're roughly the same size, same mass and
made from the same stuff.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.060
And they started out as twins.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.890
Early Venus and early Earth were very
similar.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:04.350
They were twins, probably nearly identical
twins at their earliest stages.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:11.480
Given that Venus is so Earth like in so many
ways, it's really odd that it is so different

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.170
than the Earth. And this makes it one of the
biggest mysteries in the solar system.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.580
Somewhere in their two histories.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.970
The earth. And Venus took two very different
paths.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.350
The result?

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.870
Two totally different worlds.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.560
Their paths were so different, you could
hardly believe that one would have been

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.660
related to the other.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.530
But now the opposite thing is going to
happen.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.950
We're going to catch up with our twin.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.930
We're going to evolve to be a lot more like
Venus in the future.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:49.140
In the future, the two planets paths will
converge and they will become twin like once

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:55.180
again. There is going to be hell on earth.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.570
The oceans will vaporize.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.580
The land will melt.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:07.500
Our hospitable blue planet will vanish,
replaced by a fiery molten world.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:14.290
We are actually on the earth at a time when
there's water and rain and it was so easy for

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.030
life to take hold. But that's going to
change.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.020
And take a look in at Venus and have a look
at our future.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.880
And Earth will surpass the horrors of Venus.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.660
A billion years from now, Earth could be an
unimaginably terrible place.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.170
How will this happen?

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.960
The roots of our Homeworld's destruction are
buried deep in the past of our twin planet.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:56.670
It's very much true that in studying the past
of Venus, we are also studying the distant

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.540
future of Earth.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.620
Both planets share a violent birth.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.370
Scarred by brutal planet formation.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:10.900
Giant cosmic impacts and rampant volcanism.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.010
We're trying to reconstruct things that
happened in the ancient, ancient past.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.440
It's almost like forensic planetary geology.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:27.660
4.6 billion years ago, hundreds of infant
planets begin to form around the new sun.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.490
Among them, the baby, Venus and Earth.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:42.740
And as they hurtle around the sun,
collisions are inevitable.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.600
Planet formation is like a demolition derby.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.140
In a derby. The cars are racing around a
track, going around in circles at different

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.500
speeds. What's the same thing with planets?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.060
The material is orbiting the sun.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.210
It's going around and they're all going at
different speeds, at different angles,

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:02.030
different trajectories, and sometimes boom.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.570
In this derby planet.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.620
It's planet.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.600
To become one.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.490
Violently.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.210
You have these large bodies that are hitting
each other at really high velocity.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.880
It's really very hot, violent mess.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:40.360
The amount of energy released in these
impacts is huge.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:44.830
It completely dwarfs all of the nuclear
weapons on Earth combined.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:50.470
And yet somehow on these scales you wind up
forming gigantic objects that we call

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:51.190
planets.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.670
Earth and Venus become voracious planet
eaters.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:06.500
But two spectacular collisions will set the
twins on very different paths.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:12.770
That was the moment Venus and Earth went
through this divergence to what has now

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.570
become these really dramatically different
worlds.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:21.310
The divergence begins when a mars sized
object hits Earth.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.380
The impact makes our planet spin faster.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:39.170
The core spins with it, generating a
powerful magnetic field around the planet.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.930
The field fends off the worst of the sun's
radiation.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:58.150
Around the same time, Venus takes a head on
hit from another infant planet.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:05.110
This impact explains something very weird
about Venus.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.800
Venus is actually rotating in the wrong
direction.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.110
How could that be?

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:15.760
Well, what if it got hit really hard by some
object that could do it?

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:24.970
An object so huge, Venus stops in its tracks
and begins to spin backwards.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:33.430
If you think about how much energy and what
size you need to change a planet, spin, that

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.170
is an incredibly large hit.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.460
But the backspin is slow.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:44.810
243 times slower than Earth.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.360
Without a fast spin.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:53.140
Venus's core can't generate a strong
magnetic field.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:08:00.350
It has no protection from the deadly stream
of particles blasted from the sun.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:07.930
Venus does not have a strong magnetic field,
and so it has suffered the full brunt of this

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.790
wind blasted out from the sun.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.750
The tale of two planets now splits radically.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.290
Venus will roast under a violent,
suffocating atmosphere.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:27.180
Earth will give birth to oceans.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.420
Life and intelligence.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:36.100
But ultimately, these twins fates are one
and the same.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:39.190
Earth's future is Venus.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.590
Pure hell.

